  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nGeneric method calls no longer slow down over time (#61, closes #60). An unconfigured call to a generic method stored a new imposter that could never match, and every later call scanned all of them. After a few thousand calls, each call cost about 0.5 ms. A miss now returns an imposter that is not stored, and the lookup is a plain loop instead of a LINQ chain.\n\nIndexer keys are compared with EqualityComparer\\<T>.Default (#63, closes #62). The generated indexer arguments compared keys with ==. That caused two problems:\n\nIt did not compile for unconstrained generic keys or for structs without == (CS0019).\n\nIt used reference equality for classes that override Equals, so the default indexer behaviour could not read back a value stored under an equal key.\n\nAsync methods are recognised on netstandard2.0 and .NET Framework (#65, closes #64). Task, Task\\<T> and ValueTask\\<T> were only recognised when they came from System.Runtime, System.Private.CoreLib or mscorlib. On netstandard2.0, and for ValueTask\\<T> on .NET Framework, the builders lacked ReturnsAsync/ThrowsAsync. Task types are now detected by name and namespace.\n\nCancelled builds no longer report a generator crash (#75, closes #74). A build cancelled while an imposter was being generated reported IMP005. The IDE then kept a result without the imposter until the next edit. Cancellation now propagates.\n\nGenerated file names no longer depend on attribute order (#77, closes #76). Two targets with the same name in different namespaces got IFooImposter.g.cs and IFooImposter\\_1.g.cs in processing order, so reordering the attributes swapped the files. Each file is now named after its fully qualified target, e.g. Sample.IFooImposter.g.cs, or Imposters.Sample.IFooImposter.g.cs for the dedicated namespace.\n\nPerformance\n\nFaster generator with lower memory use (#67, #69, #71):\n\nSymbol-derived syntax is cached in metadata.\n\nMethod metadata is no longer boxed.\n\nGenerated code is written in a single pass over its tokens instead of through NormalizeWhitespace.\n\nFor the 21 imposters in our sample set, generation went from about 1.2 s and 452 MB allocated to about 0.33 s and 168 MB.\n\nSmaller generated code (#73). Members that were never used are no longer emitted, including:\n\nstored imposter references in method builders;\n\nan unused invocation behaviour field;\n\nindexer getter invocation counters;\n\naccessor members that the indexer or property does not have.\n\nChanges to generated output\n\nGenerated files use tab indentation and LF line endings (#71). The layout is otherwise unchanged.\n\nGenerated file names include the target's namespace (#77). If you inspect the files through EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles, they now appear under the new names.",
